(G) WHY W'' <= 2/3 ?  test  rho >= 3P  (P = # mirror pairs)
==============================================================================
  P  |  min rho observed  |  witness           |  3P  |  rho>=3P
  1  |  3                |  (1, 2, 3)         |  3   |  yes
  2  |  6                |  (5, 6, 23)        |  6   |  yes
  3  |  14               |  (1, 13, 14)       |  9   |  yes
  4  |  17               |  (1, 16, 17)       |  12  |  yes
  5  |  21               |  (1, 20, 21)       |  15  |  yes
  directions violating rho >= 3P : 0 
  NOTE rho >= 3P  =>  sum over pairs of 1/rho <= P/(3P) = 1/3  =>  W'' <= 2/3.

  IMPLICATION: sojourn <= (1/7)*W'' always (C+F).  If W'' <= 2/3 is a theorem,
  then sojourn <= 2/21 for EVERY direction -- no split on mirror pairs, so
  death-star's >=2-pair residue closes too.
